# Added 2026-08-28. The delivery had none, so a `git add .` would have committed every
# dependency tree in it -- `pnpm install` alone writes ~200 MB under front-end/node_modules.
node_modules/

# Generated by `svelte-kit sync` and by the build. Both are reproducible from source.
.svelte-kit/
build/

# Playwright output.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# ⚠️ NO `.env` FILE IS EVER COMMITTED, in either project, whatever is in it.
#
# The front-end's keys are all `PUBLIC_*`, so they are compiled into the client bundle and are
# already readable by anyone who loads the page. That makes their VALUES harmless and is not a
# reason to track the file: a committed `.env` is where somebody later adds a real credential,
# and GitHub's push protection flags the filename without reading it. The checked-in artifact is
# `front-end/.env.example`, which a fresh clone copies.
.env
*.env
!*.env.example

# Never commit data derived from MIMIC-IV: it is credentialed under a PhysioNet DUA.
*.csv
